# No workspace tab collapse suggestions

When proposing usability improvements for ArchLucid review workspaces, **do not** suggest:

- Hiding "rare" desktop review workspace tabs behind a **More** menu or overflow
- Collapsing table-style tab strips to reduce visible tab count
- Demoting primary workspace sections into disclosure solely to shrink the tab bar

## Why

Review workspace tabs are the primary navigation model for in-review work. Collapsing them trades scanability for marginal chrome savings and has been explicitly rejected by product direction.

## What to do instead

Prefer improvements that:

- Clarify tab labels and ordering without removing tabs from the default strip
- Improve mobile-specific patterns (e.g. select-based **More sections**) where viewport constraints already justify a different control
- Reduce duplicate CTAs, unify search, or consolidate header actions — without hiding core workspace tabs on desktop

## Scope

Applies to assessment batches, usability suggestion lists, and agent prompts for review detail / workspace chrome — not to unrelated collapsible UI (metadata disclosures, advanced lists, optional intake paths).
